et_id":"29a3-117b-b8f9-4cf3"},{"link_uuid":"9cc520c8-9e1c-4ea2-bf49-c78cbedd7f9e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"565a-f0cb-e9f4-46ce"},{"link_uuid":"11685e31-2e0d-45da-96cc-36641733a814","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"68ad-f56e-10cd-4bef"},{"link_uuid":"756f89e6-959f-4878-858c-f6dc30cfc4ee","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"f9ee-9464-0499-40f4"},{"link_uuid":"e28741ed-41b5-4320-8667-95f8071fea35","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e673-5d7d-1888-4f76"},{"link_uuid":"f2c794d8-4cd9-4e5c-a375-f33c69ba85de","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e18e-7b67-b2ed-4039"},{"link_uuid":"48d993ca-92f7-456d-8edc-6315e02a868e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"85a2-32f0-e6f1-4860"},{"link_uuid":"b312e621-6125-4892-bb7e-780f58b9fe2a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e02d-b103-dc4a-48cb"},{"link_uuid":"0d0d3962-dcdc-400a-8fb0-b1600bb1a2e2","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"5a03-d9ce-928d-4cb1"},{"link_uuid":"7bbb7b1d-f854-4a19-a120-4cc38ce63934","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"3f17-9a27-a083-4abf"},{"link_uuid":"095e378f-5a5f-459f-8433-4f61861b9a7a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c5ef-7236-e2ee-4899"},{"link_uuid":"30b27e54-0e58-4cd4-bf28-73b8bfe7b3a5","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c33e-b13c-49b0-42c2"},{"link_uuid":"26f75f5b-bf39-48cb-82a2-74ebcd29fd26","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"30f2-e998-fad1-40e5"},{"link_uuid":"57ffb56c-53d2-4558-bb02-411a39e22dbb","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8bb6-c3db-2148-431c"},{"link_uuid":"240eca42-ac2b-43f6-9931-2faf7ce56add","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"5ee5-41c1-7788-4065"},{"link_uuid":"d4b55124-f569-4b68-91a6-88dfc05b46bf","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"5ba2-e837-df9f-4a0e"},{"link_uuid":"bad18545-dc90-4243-874c-2e5f68f8e6de","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"493c-2dc8-2d10-47f0"},{"link_uuid":"129305cf-c543-41af-bb51-ad7894d424b3","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"dc2a-8bc3-7ce0-4131"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/unit cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_fixture_selection_corpus.py:1-11, 167-172` — Preserve corpus-wide selection behavior. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_fixture_selection_escape_index.py:1-15` — Preserve escaped-index selection behavior. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_fixture_selection_heldout.py:1-9` — Preserve independent selection coverage. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_fixture_selection.py:1-9` — Preserve fixture-selection precedence. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_flaky_test_guidance.py:1-13, 72-77` — Preserve the no-blind-retry guidance contract. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_fold_orphan_laundering.py:1-27, 168-170` — Preserve rejection of orphan laundering during fold. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_g5_decomp_det.py:1-15` — Preserve G5 decomposition determinism. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_gate_admission_09da.py:133-137` — Preserve the gate-admission edge case. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_gate_context_seam.py:1-18, 32-37, 78-82, 101-104, 112-117, 160-164` — Preserve gate-context injection and stable test seams. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_gate_dispatch_seam.py:1-14, 96-101, 118-121` — Preserve dispatch indirection and monkeypatch compatibility. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_gate_engine_cutover.py:44-49, 168-178` — Preserve exclusive use of the current gate engine and legacy-path rejection. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_gate_peak_rss_9ea3.py:1-19, 98-102, 203-217` — Preserve peak-RSS accounting and bounded-memory thresholds. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py:1-32, 149-154` — Preserve bounded scratch-volume behavior and cleanup. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_gate_source_defaults_repo_root.py:32-42` — Preserve repo-root defaulting for gate sources. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_gate_state_tristate_f5c4.py:1-14, 93-98` — Preserve the three distinct gate states. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_gate_step_id_validation.py:1-19, 115-122` — Preserve strict gate-step identifier validation and diagnostics. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_gate_step_tree_skew.py:1-25, 42-50, 53-56, 160-165` — Preserve step resolution against the intended tree/ref. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_gate_store_freshness.py:1-17, 57-61, 170-176, 245-250` — Preserve stale-store detection and refresh ordering. Consumer: test maintainers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_fixture_selection_corpus.py tests/unit/test_fixture_selection_escape_index.py tests/unit/test_fixture_selection_heldout.py tests/unit/test_fixture_selection.py